# Production build settings. Tracked on purpose — everything a Vite env var
# holds ends up in the shipped bundle, so nothing secret may live here.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# `.env` is gitignored, so it is whatever the person building happens to have
# on their machine — usually `VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8787/api/v1` for
# `npm run dev`. Vite loads `.env` in EVERY mode, so `npm run build` baked that
# localhost URL into the production bundle, and the deployed app asked the
# user's own phone for the API. Every request failed with status 0 and the app
# looked like the server was down.
#
# Vite gives `.env.production` precedence over `.env` when building, so this
# file makes the shipped bundle correct no matter what the builder has locally.

# RELATIVE, deliberately. The app and the API share an origin: nginx proxies
# /api/ to the Node process on the same host, so the browser must ask whatever
# host it loaded the page from. An absolute URL here would hard-code one
# deployment's domain into the bundle and break every other one.
VITE_API_URL=/api/v1

# Empty means "use the default", which is the models served beside the app.
VITE_MODEL_BASE_URL=
